 "script": "US gas prices rose nine point one percent in a single month. That pushed inflation to three point seven percent, the Labor Department said Wednesday. Gasoline caused more than half of September's increase. The Iran war has disrupted oil supplies since late February. Here's the part that hits your wallet. In September, gas cost thirty-four point two percent more than a year earlier. Food prices were flat last month. Fed officials, who raised rates in September, expect one more hike this year. What do you pay for a gallon where you live? Tell us below.",
